<LegalPage lang="en" title="Privacy policy | Codex Handbook" description="How Codex Handbook handles necessary access data, cookieless analytics, and local browser settings." canonical="https://codexhandbook.com/en/privacy-policy/">
<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p>Codex Handbook is a public content website. We do not require readers to create an account or submit personal information on its pages.</p>
<h2>Access data</h2><p>To deliver pages, hosting and network infrastructure process necessary request data such as IP addresses, requested URLs, browser or device information, and error logs.</p>
<h2>Cookieless analytics</h2><p>The site automatically loads Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity in cookieless mode. Analytics storage, advertising storage, advertising user data, and ad personalization stay denied. The services receive basic page-view and interaction data, but the site does not create analytics cookies or show an analytics consent banner or settings panel.</p>
<h2>Browser settings</h2><p>The site may use local browser storage to remember your theme choice. This setting stays in your browser and is not sent to third-party analytics or advertising services.</p>
<h2>External links</h2><p>The site links to OpenAI documentation, GitHub, and other resources. When visiting an external site, refer to that service’s privacy policy.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, use the GitHub channels listed on the <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
<p>Last updated: <time datetime={updatedAt}>{updatedAt}</time></p>
</LegalPage>
